-- title:
--   Algebraisation of a crossing chart: nodal completion and horizontal primes
-- statement:
--   Setting. Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume: `hpM`, $p \mid M$; `hpM2`, $p^{2} \nmid M$; `hHp`, every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` for the divisibility $M/p \mid M$ is $1$ lies in $H$; and $M/p \neq 0$. Assume `hj`: the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`. Let `𝔛 : XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` be a model package for $X_H(M)$ over the ring `R p`; among its components are properness, flatness, integrality and local finite presentation of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` together with normality of the affine charts, the corresponding proper smooth data at the auxiliary level `ΓN p M H hpM`, and a curve model `𝔛.Meta : CurveModel (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥(xHFunctionFieldBar M H)` (an integral proper smooth curve `𝔛.Meta.C` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with an isomorphism `𝔛.Meta.ffEquiv` of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` onto its function field and a bijection between its closed points and the places of that field) together with an isomorphism `𝔛.eeta` of `𝔛.Meta.C` onto the base change `pullback (toBase p (ΓM M H) hj) (Spec.map (algebraMap (R p) (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)))`, Galois compatibility and a normalisation of the finite chart.
--
--   Base data. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime p`, that is $p$ lies in the non-units of $A$, whose residue field is of characteristic $p$ and algebraically closed, and let $\rho :$ `R p` $\to A$ satisfy `hρ`: composing $\rho$ with the inclusion $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ gives the structure map of `R p`. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, with a map $\rho_O :$ `R p` $\to O$, such that `hϖ`: the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by $p$; let `toκ : O →+* ResidueField ↥A` satisfy `htoκ`, $\mathrm{toκ} \circ \rho_O = \mathrm{residue} \circ \rho$; let `jO : O →+* AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfy `hjO`, $j_O \circ \rho_O$ is the structure map of `R p`; and let `ιA : O →+* ↥A` satisfy `hιA`, the inclusion $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ after $\iota_A$ equals $j_O$, and `hιAκ`, $\mathrm{residue} \circ \iota_A = \mathrm{toκ}$.
--
--   The crossing. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` and `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` supplied by the package, and write $x_n$ for the image of $n$ in `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` (the base change of the model to $O$) under `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρO toκ htoκ`, the latter being the map of the fibre over the residue field of $A$ into the $O$-model induced by `toκ`.
--
--   Chart data. Let $e \ge 1$, let $U$ be an open of `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` with `hxU`: $x_n \in U$, and let
--   $$f : U \longrightarrow \mathrm{Spec}\bigl(O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - p^{e})\bigr)$$
--   be a morphism to `CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme (((p : ℕ) : O) ^ e)`. The hypotheses on $f$ are: `hover`, $f$ followed by the structural morphism to $\mathrm{Spec}\,O$ equals $U.\iota$ followed by `pullback.snd`, so $f$ is a morphism over $\mathrm{Spec}\,O$; `hfib`, for $y \in U$ the two distinguished elements `CrossingQuotient.U (p^e)` and `CrossingQuotient.V (p^e)` both lie in the prime $f.\mathrm{base}\,y$ if and only if the image of $y$ in the model is $x_n$; `hpt`, at every $y$ lying over $x_n$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal, and induces an isomorphism of residue fields; `het`, every such $y$ has an open neighbourhood $V$ in $U$ with $V.\iota$ followed by $f$ étale; and the four conditions `hor₁`–`hor₄`, which say that for $y \in U$ the element `CrossingQuotient.V (p^e)` lies in $f.\mathrm{base}\,y$ exactly when the image of $y$ lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 0` followed by `bcMap …`, and `CrossingQuotient.U (p^e)` lies in $f.\mathrm{base}\,y$ exactly when that image lies in the range of `𝔛.comp A hA ρ hρ 1` followed by `bcMap …`.
--
--   Notation in the conclusion. Put `XQ` for the base change `pullback (toBase p (ΓM M H) hj) (Spec.map (algebraMap (R p) (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)))` and `prJ : XQ ⟶ XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` for the morphism induced by $j_O$ (the identity on the model, $\mathrm{Spec}\,j_O$ on the base); `VM` denotes the open `𝔛.eeta ⁻¹ᵁ (prJ ⁻¹ᵁ U)` of `𝔛.Meta.C`. Put $Q :=$ `CrossingQuotient O (p^e)`, let $\varphi$ be the identification of $Q$ with the global sections of `crossingScheme (p^e)`, and let
--   $$g_v, g_u \in \Gamma\bigl(\mathrm{XO}(\Gamma_M, hj, \rho_O),\ U.\iota\,''^{U}\,\top\bigr)$$
--   be the sections obtained by pulling back $\varphi(\mathrm{V}(p^e))$ and $\varphi(\mathrm{U}(p^e))$ along $f$ and transporting through the isomorphism `U.ι.appIso ⊤`. Under the further hypothesis `hgen` that the generic point of `𝔛.Meta.C` lies in `𝔛.eeta ⁻¹ᵁ (prJ ⁻¹ᵁ (U.ι ''ᵁ ⊤))`, let
--   $$\mathrm{read} : \Gamma\bigl(\mathrm{XO},\ U.\iota\,''^{U}\,\top\bigr) \to \ ↥(\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\ M\ H)$$
--   be the ring homomorphism given by restricting along `prJ`, then along `𝔛.eeta`, then taking the germ at the generic point of `𝔛.Meta.C`, then transporting through `𝔛.Meta.ffEquiv.symm`; and set $\mathrm{param} := \mathrm{read}\,g_v$ and $\mathrm{param}' := \mathrm{read}\,g_u$.
--
--   Conclusion. For every $g \in$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` there exist:
--
--   — a discrete valuation ring $O'$ which is a domain, an element $\varpi'$ generating its maximal ideal, and an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota_A' : O' \to A$;
--
--   — a Noetherian local domain $B$, a local ring homomorphism $\sigma_B : O' \to B$, and an injective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{emb} : B \to$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`;
--
--   — a discrete valuation ring $W'$ which is a domain and is adically complete for its maximal ideal, an irreducible element $\pi'$ of $W'$, an integer $E' \ge 1$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$\iota' : \widehat{B} = \mathrm{AdicCompletion}(\mathfrak m_B, B) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W'\ (\pi'^{E'}),$$
--   the target being the quotient of $W'[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W' (π'^E')`;
--
--   — a unit $w_0$ of that quotient such that $\iota'$ carries the image of $\sigma_B \varpi'$ in $\widehat{B}$ to $w_0 \cdot$ `UVCrossingModel.const (π'^E') π'`, the class of the constant power series $\pi'$;
--
--   — elements $b_u, b_v \in B$ and a unit $w_u$ of the quotient such that $\iota'$ carries the image of $b_u$ to `UVCrossingModel.U (π'^E')` $\cdot\, w_u$ and the image of $b_v$ to `UVCrossingModel.V (π'^E')`, together with $\mathrm{emb}\,b_v = \mathrm{param}$ and $\mathrm{emb}\,b_u = \mathrm{param}'$;
--
--   — a presentation of $g$ as a fraction from $B$: elements $r, s \in B$ with $s \neq 0$ and $g \cdot \mathrm{emb}\,s = \mathrm{emb}\,r$;
--
--   — a commutative ring $S$ and a ring homomorphism $j_A : A \to S$ along which unit multiples descend: whenever $j_A\alpha = j_A\beta \cdot u$ with $\alpha,\beta \in A$ and $u \in S^{\times}$, there is $v \in A^{\times}$ with $\alpha = \beta v$;
--
--   such that the following two statements hold.
--
--   (1) For every place $W$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — that is, a valuation subring of that field containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, distinct from the whole field and a principal ideal ring — which is rational in the sense that $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ surjects onto its residue field, and for every morphism $s : \mathrm{Spec}\,A \to U$ such that $s$ followed by $U.\iota$ followed by `pullback.snd` equals $\mathrm{Spec}\,\iota_A$, such that `barPt A` followed by $s$ and $U.\iota$ equals the section `(𝔛.Meta.pointEquivPlace.symm W).1` followed by `𝔛.eeta` and `prJ`, and such that the image of the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ under $s$ and $U.\iota$ is $x_n$: there exist ring homomorphisms $\chi : B \to A$ and $\psi : \widehat{B} \to S$ with $\chi$ local, $\chi \circ \sigma_B = \iota_A'$, $\psi \circ (B \to \widehat{B}) = j_A \circ \chi$, such that for every $b \in B$ the element $\mathrm{emb}\,b$ lies in the valuation subring of $W$ and $W.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{emb}\,b)$ equals the image of $\chi b$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and such that every $x$ in the valuation subring of $W$ which is a fraction from $B$ (so $x \cdot \mathrm{emb}\,s_0 = \mathrm{emb}\,r$ for some $r, s_0 \in B$ with $s_0 \neq 0$) admits such a presentation with denominator outside the kernel of $\chi$: there are $r, s_0 \in B$ with $\chi s_0 \neq 0$ and $x \cdot \mathrm{emb}\,s_0 = \mathrm{emb}\,r$.
--
--   (2) Conversely, for every prime ideal $P$ of $B$ with $P \neq 0$ and $\sigma_B \varpi' \notin P$ there exist a rational place $W$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a morphism $s : \mathrm{Spec}\,A \to U$ satisfying the same three conditions as in (1) (compatibility with $\mathrm{Spec}\,\iota_A$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,O$, agreement of the induced $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point with the point of `𝔛.Meta.C` corresponding to $W$, and specialisation of the closed point to $x_n$), and a ring homomorphism $\chi : B \to A$ which is local, satisfies $\chi \circ \sigma_B = \iota_A'$, satisfies for all $b \in B$ that $\mathrm{emb}\,b$ lies in the valuation subring of $W$ with $W.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{emb}\,b)$ the image of $\chi b$, and has the denominator property of (1), and which in addition cuts out $P$: for all $b \in B$, $b \in P$ if and only if $\chi b = 0$.
--
--   This is the algebraisation step for the local picture at a crossing point of the fibre at $p$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$: the étale chart $f$ onto $\mathrm{Spec}\,O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1-p^e)$ is converted into a Noetherian local domain $B$, sitting inside the geometric function field and large enough to contain a prescribed element $g$ as a fraction, whose adic completion is a nodal power series ring $W'[[X_0,X_1]]/(\,\cdot\,)$ in which the two chart coordinates become the standard ones, together with a dictionary identifying the nonzero primes of $B$ not containing $\sigma_B\varpi'$ with the rational places specialising to the crossing. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_zpow_unit_principle_evalAt_read_chart_of_section_of_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_zpow_unit_principle_evalAt_read_chart_of_section_of_chart), the unit principle for values of sections on the annulus around the crossing.
